[{:db/id "q-42041/selection/dc82e55d00f9249e3bd7049c307da7622f635c9b050e775d45eacbf5ab709aac" :answer/id #uuid "41109a43-3c87-59ca-bcc7-229b8a8eb449" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+4z \\\\ 3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42041/selection/4caa2e10ee20e6b623a1d95e588d5f2ab074c28349743a0c817ea80088f67b3c" :answer/id #uuid "a74658ab-6621-565d-8a89-7358301574eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2+4z \\\\ 1-3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42041/selection/699575fb67d8d7c75cbc4d4b1f46c4cbaa2ba24ea7bdcae1fdf2ede1e90bfff8" :answer/id #uuid "192b6da6-515a-5d39-94fe-459d8d85fff9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+2z \\\\ -3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42041/selection/a2245a39f5e0f5d242c6b25f4649d75c47dbabeafa7e403862cca6eca09b75e6" :answer/id #uuid "d956ce98-8354-52ea-b7e2-6f47d9302574" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2z \\\\ 4z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42041/selection/b3536d73d94c987c885e84903024a0b5aa3a72efccc85ab4b0bd3258c302a648" :answer/id #uuid "289b5e1b-d5de-5cd8-a853-a1325eb3ba0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2+4z \\\\ -3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42041/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cc7d8608-6cac-5579-9b7d-8a78b7ebbee6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-42041/selection/699575fb67d8d7c75cbc4d4b1f46c4cbaa2ba24ea7bdcae1fdf2ede1e90bfff8" :answer-field/choices ["q-42041/selection/dc82e55d00f9249e3bd7049c307da7622f635c9b050e775d45eacbf5ab709aac" "q-42041/selection/4caa2e10ee20e6b623a1d95e588d5f2ab074c28349743a0c817ea80088f67b3c" "q-42041/selection/699575fb67d8d7c75cbc4d4b1f46c4cbaa2ba24ea7bdcae1fdf2ede1e90bfff8" "q-42041/selection/a2245a39f5e0f5d242c6b25f4649d75c47dbabeafa7e403862cca6eca09b75e6" "q-42041/selection/b3536d73d94c987c885e84903024a0b5aa3a72efccc85ab4b0bd3258c302a648"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-42041" :question/id #uuid "09fe1174-4802-515f-8d41-d02fb865fb55" :question/math-academy-id "q-42041" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-4z=2 \\\\ 4x+y-5z=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2z=1 \\\\ y+3z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1+2z \\\\ y=-3z \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+2z \\\\ -3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-42041/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d81e3f1-d930-59ee-b439-2a3645aebb6c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-42041"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131712/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67" :answer/id #uuid "56836203-c4be-53e9-b541-53a7bedc87b1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131712/selection/e38129464679d925329512a145c313121728d6433bb30ea42ac6f758a6d70e26" :answer/id #uuid "ee8a01d4-8cb1-5cd3-a55e-21515404bc40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3-4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131712/selection/9877e11a1aefb73ab1c4d2438201e7dd8093d721c2555a79acca7149c5b161dc" :answer/id #uuid "abf4b289-daed-5182-a993-644d739be96c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4y-3 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131712/selection/d7c128652dd95bef9c980132e748fc815a595e6287663fb7ba2888bfb54c905d" :answer/id #uuid "922b9afb-4edf-5afd-926d-9a8590705ddd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4y-3 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131712/selection/a995914454e5e87c5137c56aa36778690e00584d2e41759e9794cdd57d5e16cd" :answer/id #uuid "c4f6f0f7-d6ab-508e-9ece-17d869f2c1cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4y+3 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131712/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c94cbe09-bdb3-5177-b965-eab79df51cb6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131712/selection/9877e11a1aefb73ab1c4d2438201e7dd8093d721c2555a79acca7149c5b161dc" :answer-field/choices ["q-131712/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67" "q-131712/selection/e38129464679d925329512a145c313121728d6433bb30ea42ac6f758a6d70e26" "q-131712/selection/9877e11a1aefb73ab1c4d2438201e7dd8093d721c2555a79acca7149c5b161dc" "q-131712/selection/d7c128652dd95bef9c980132e748fc815a595e6287663fb7ba2888bfb54c905d" "q-131712/selection/a995914454e5e87c5137c56aa36778690e00584d2e41759e9794cdd57d5e16cd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131712" :question/id #uuid "b0feb9ee-8e97-5292-aff6-05655689f05b" :question/math-academy-id "q-131712" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+8y=-6 \\\\  & -4x-16y=12 \\\\  & 6x+24y=-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 & -6 \\\\ -4 & -16 & 12 \\\\ 6 & 24 & -18\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 & -6 \\\\ -4 & -16 & 12 \\\\ 6 & 24 & -18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -16 & 12 \\\\ 6 & 24 & -18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 24 & -18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+4y=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we need to find $x$  in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-4y-3 \\\\ y=y,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4y-3 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-131712/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d81e3f1-d930-59ee-b439-2a3645aebb6c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131712"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131717/selection/ec57be106bfc4230432f9d0925d7bb366e3e8cc1470a16093e843e13b280307e" :answer/id #uuid "0c30fead-4a73-5022-9e9a-21dd0b0638a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{3}-4 \\\\ 1-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131717/selection/c096d8d9fd57eb2b627f123302ee468c06bcd32b95a32d11c9286613d734f601" :answer/id #uuid "d6d2bc07-7dc8-55a2-81a6-b1489f131d1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{3}+4 \\\\ 2{x}_{3}+1 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131717/selection/3e48f131da63afc3ccf6c17d11d6ad5ecfbe0ed5e3fb607c743baabd02d5ca19" :answer/id #uuid "59bbb71e-60d8-5eae-8d64-214b3d7c235e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{3}-4 \\\\ 2{x}_{3}-1 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131717/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67" :answer/id #uuid "18dc88f8-bcb4-52ae-adfb-a82167f7d74d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131717/selection/11a3033683847fedebec8900765b0fffb053014da61dd19091d42c149d6d74c2" :answer/id #uuid "f763111a-5af4-5488-a929-0020e0aeba2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4-5{x}_{3} \\\\ 1-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131717/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0efdee88-6a7c-5974-993d-2ab3cf0ff497" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131717/selection/ec57be106bfc4230432f9d0925d7bb366e3e8cc1470a16093e843e13b280307e" :answer-field/choices ["q-131717/selection/ec57be106bfc4230432f9d0925d7bb366e3e8cc1470a16093e843e13b280307e" "q-131717/selection/c096d8d9fd57eb2b627f123302ee468c06bcd32b95a32d11c9286613d734f601" "q-131717/selection/3e48f131da63afc3ccf6c17d11d6ad5ecfbe0ed5e3fb607c743baabd02d5ca19" "q-131717/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67" "q-131717/selection/11a3033683847fedebec8900765b0fffb053014da61dd19091d42c149d6d74c2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131717" :question/id #uuid "ea253a83-404b-5d27-8e99-ab1346327cc6" :question/math-academy-id "q-131717" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -5 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}-5{x}_{3}=-4 \\\\  & {x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ and we have one free variable, ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ in terms of ${x}_{3}.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=5{x}_{3}-4 \\\\ {x}_{2}=1-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}={x}_{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{3}$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{3}-4 \\\\ 1-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-131717/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d81e3f1-d930-59ee-b439-2a3645aebb6c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131717"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-42019/selection/1f17e16ec07b68e484cfa342e367b549bdb532e68c27de0fdd72a1c248216742" :answer/id #uuid "c8fb9412-eb4b-5fc7-a668-6254be1176b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2-z \\\\ 0 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42019/selection/c3e01517f5a4e6c5fd5345e1bae604281f6474fae43a2c005b8ae95af9d39f91" :answer/id #uuid "3a715954-196e-5121-9eb2-a071e7214ff8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ z-1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42019/selection/d60bbcdf4d7a6342027d376be51c629dc69d33bd146af71c05840d5abc0264f7" :answer/id #uuid "118b2c2b-be06-5fce-b85e-7beb4cab4232" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42019/selection/2dd8d505d599e7135fed25096caa60213aab7546bb53036ca403ed43f922b5d8" :answer/id #uuid "43677cd0-73bf-5272-95a1-c7d210e1257c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-z \\\\ z-1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42019/selection/2cea86482460683778d27f17627022f4ccb8055927a14809d48089e2674752b7" :answer/id #uuid "180aa355-38f3-5bc4-a98d-6089535eaac0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1-z \\\\ 0 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42019/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "47bbcdd9-b23e-52e8-94f0-96d651969d9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-42019/selection/c3e01517f5a4e6c5fd5345e1bae604281f6474fae43a2c005b8ae95af9d39f91" :answer-field/choices ["q-42019/selection/1f17e16ec07b68e484cfa342e367b549bdb532e68c27de0fdd72a1c248216742" "q-42019/selection/c3e01517f5a4e6c5fd5345e1bae604281f6474fae43a2c005b8ae95af9d39f91" "q-42019/selection/d60bbcdf4d7a6342027d376be51c629dc69d33bd146af71c05840d5abc0264f7" "q-42019/selection/2dd8d505d599e7135fed25096caa60213aab7546bb53036ca403ed43f922b5d8" "q-42019/selection/2cea86482460683778d27f17627022f4ccb8055927a14809d48089e2674752b7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-42019" :question/id #uuid "013e11bb-39c0-595b-a244-03847638286f" :question/math-academy-id "q-42019" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-2y+2z=2 \\\\  & y-z=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x=0 \\\\  & y-z=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=0 \\\\ y=z-1 \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ z-1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-42019/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d81e3f1-d930-59ee-b439-2a3645aebb6c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-42019"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-32244/selection/e53d600e5ac2a950643d2ce8b3582c7c2f5895adace73a99aa50295882f05b31" :answer/id #uuid "fd41b690-20e8-52dc-8c3c-9bb0f646fd6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{5}-2 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32244/selection/87707b4e5809eaa7b85749ca55c2b117d4cc669e07f758424d05ae2411bcf7fc" :answer/id #uuid "e07c84d7-1589-5805-8860-fbb861e4c39d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2}-y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32244/selection/9856bfa2403e782aa4c499bf15095f42b76f286a7311d397a7103340837f3b43" :answer/id #uuid "99cbd0d8-7b09-5efa-8f17-201122c25a1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2}+x \\\\ x\\end{aligned}],\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32244/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67" :answer/id #uuid "c55855e4-fc66-5d64-a2b1-efb507fec362" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32244/selection/2a764b02f4d326adaea395a1d4e8554ca0e742b2d817346c669419ea2d7f001f" :answer/id #uuid "9e7a5b67-f13d-5ecd-9c55-04bf75ad9f6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5-y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32244/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f1b6f7cb-18ee-5250-a3f9-3c9d6c108b8c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-32244/selection/87707b4e5809eaa7b85749ca55c2b117d4cc669e07f758424d05ae2411bcf7fc" :answer-field/choices ["q-32244/selection/e53d600e5ac2a950643d2ce8b3582c7c2f5895adace73a99aa50295882f05b31" "q-32244/selection/87707b4e5809eaa7b85749ca55c2b117d4cc669e07f758424d05ae2411bcf7fc" "q-32244/selection/9856bfa2403e782aa4c499bf15095f42b76f286a7311d397a7103340837f3b43" "q-32244/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67" "q-32244/selection/2a764b02f4d326adaea395a1d4e8554ca0e742b2d817346c669419ea2d7f001f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-32244" :question/id #uuid "02a48d7a-4163-5713-bdfc-4c30a3ac1491" :question/math-academy-id "q-32244" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+2y=5 \\\\  & -10x-10y=-25 \\\\  & 8x+8y=20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 5 \\\\ -10 & -10 & -25 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 20\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 5 \\\\ -10 & -10 & -25 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 20\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -10 & -10 & -25 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 20\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+10{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 20\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-8){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y=\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we need to find $x$  in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{5}{2}-y \\\\ y=y,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2}-y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-32244/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d81e3f1-d930-59ee-b439-2a3645aebb6c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-32244"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131724/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "9bd15515-5743-5020-981f-7c4b2f450897" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131724/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "b51758dc-7f53-57bf-92cf-0283d4a01944" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131724/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "1c0b9397-ce4f-5728-b49f-219395f94aac" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131724/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "78a929b9-0473-539f-beb7-2bbefc400063" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131724/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "e6b7640a-48ae-5763-9b0d-2ea31e3bb516" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131724/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "43dbb445-b54a-5c1b-aa3d-7705c663ae63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131724/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-131724/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-131724/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-131724/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-131724/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-131724/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131724" :question/id #uuid "e93f981b-b1bd-511a-87f1-b614c74c85ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-131724" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-2y=2 \\\\  & -3x-4y=3 \\\\  & 2x-4y=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is consistent dependent\n- The system has a unique solution\n- The system is inconsistent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 9 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=-5,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-131724/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131724"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-42020/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "9eaa3d19-5e97-5969-be15-6d2f7e90d195" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42020/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "233786e0-6b57-514b-998e-fa7d6da6c104" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42020/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "f6ff5d69-7707-5b49-863c-a61832e1f51b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42020/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "14e5e29b-adbe-5916-bfa3-e152421f2417" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42020/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "b8035881-063f-5748-82a7-e8e17c4d482c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42020/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "daf102e0-7cc7-5eb1-8770-e5338389ece2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-42020/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-42020/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-42020/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-42020/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-42020/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-42020/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-42020" :question/id #uuid "1a930b2a-2578-5145-8e40-06b6cab16ba9" :question/math-academy-id "q-42020" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y=-1 \\\\  & 3x+y=3 \\\\  & -2x+y=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is consistent dependent\n- The system has a unique solution\n- The system is inconsistent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=2,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-42020/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-42020"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131719/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "4e841753-e6ff-5ea7-b26f-6d9575329fa9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131719/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "33e69ce1-6954-5201-8c9c-5e864e29e461" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131719/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "a5ba308b-dbba-56f5-baa5-466e5aeb13fe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131719/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "f81946b8-0e51-5d2c-a843-bc2231e1d145" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131719/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "2e3ae4ee-b56e-5f4e-aae8-59dacc65408d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131719/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "33fce12e-12f7-5945-a801-72dea6bcf2e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131719/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-131719/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-131719/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-131719/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-131719/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-131719/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131719" :question/id #uuid "85139672-fc12-5f19-974e-cd9c9c3f59d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-131719" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+4y=-1 \\\\  & 2x+8y=-2 \\\\  & -3x-12y=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is inconsistent\n- The system is consistent dependent\n- The system has a unique solution" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x,$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we can find $x$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-131719/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131719"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131722/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "908a019e-8258-54e1-a3e6-de86654a1050" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131722/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "4b8dd03f-0f8a-5866-a7eb-663a28f92dd6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131722/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "ea552307-27bc-5f39-aeb6-7cbb6673ebb6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131722/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "d27cbb7b-ab8d-5431-b448-c300eaa43995" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131722/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "1e6537cf-4f5d-52e6-94e3-f493b4f11925" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131722/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b05a5f36-6352-563f-aae4-29464953bae5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131722/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-131722/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-131722/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-131722/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-131722/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-131722/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131722" :question/id #uuid "4890e1ff-ed9a-5558-acd1-bcef01439e04" :question/math-academy-id "q-131722" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 3x-3y=6 \\\\  & -2x+y=-3 \\\\  & 4x-4y=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is consistent dependent\n- The system is consistent independent\n- The system has no solution" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y=2 \\\\ y=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we have $y=-1$ and substituting this into the first equation yields $x=1.$ So,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-131722/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131722"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-42061"] :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-3y+z=0 \\\\  & -4x+6y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is consistent dependent\n- The system has no solution\n- The system is consistent independent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 6 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 6 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we can to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement I is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-131729/selection/b1ccbf8f5fca543d6c97f5378c2c6cb667ff8c4bfd4e1a16108985d75e9f613a" :answer/id #uuid "8bcc81a2-c947-5975-aeea-d4f7abb1d8de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131729/selection/026331c8f5499d14868070120d8faf28f7908963b78fddd1e0abe32f8c18d39e" :answer/id #uuid "2bfe9ef6-dcef-5d1c-89ab-085d758feff3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-\\frac{2}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131729/selection/2288413a383e153ad9acb6430532cecdb55509b55573ff6fd9f6b1db345a1152" :answer/id #uuid "8d98839c-b0ac-51c1-aa1e-3f5c9668efe6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131729/selection/f9a36dc20554097250ff0324e179977bb892219ae9b27b5c2ca8864aac6c0450" :answer/id #uuid "f90fd90e-4c48-5dc4-88a5-2254307f1681" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131729/selection/10cc2e6b77a33cb5d48301a9259f3f24396757207b802415d22dafe1586468e3" :answer/id #uuid "4a162357-d3eb-5b79-a136-8f7482a4d4a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131729/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "01c086ee-bd59-5116-96cd-3ea346830057" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131729/selection/b1ccbf8f5fca543d6c97f5378c2c6cb667ff8c4bfd4e1a16108985d75e9f613a" :answer-field/choices ["q-131729/selection/b1ccbf8f5fca543d6c97f5378c2c6cb667ff8c4bfd4e1a16108985d75e9f613a" "q-131729/selection/026331c8f5499d14868070120d8faf28f7908963b78fddd1e0abe32f8c18d39e" "q-131729/selection/2288413a383e153ad9acb6430532cecdb55509b55573ff6fd9f6b1db345a1152" "q-131729/selection/f9a36dc20554097250ff0324e179977bb892219ae9b27b5c2ca8864aac6c0450" "q-131729/selection/10cc2e6b77a33cb5d48301a9259f3f24396757207b802415d22dafe1586468e3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131729" :question/id #uuid "676ffc31-b8a6-5563-a4f4-246e28e53f8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-131729" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is consistent dependent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & -2x+7y=6 \\\\  & x+ky=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 7 & 6 \\\\ 1 & k & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 7 & 6 \\\\ 1 & k & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & k & -3 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & k & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2k+7 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+ky=-3 \\\\  & (2k+7)y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is consistent dependent if it has infinitely many solutions. For the system to have infinitely many solutions, it must have at least one free variable.\n\nIf $k=-\\frac{7}{2},$ then the second equation is $0=0,$ which is true for any value of $y$, and we can remove this equation from the system. As a result, the system will contain only one equation, $x+ky=-3.$ \n\nThen, the basic variable will be $x,$ and we will have a free variable $y.$ That means the system will have infinitely many solutions.\n\nTherefore, our system is consistent dependent when $k=-\\frac{7}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-131729/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "22733f71-de4a-5058-a41c-039e66e333c5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131729"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-32246"] :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is consistent dependent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 3x+4y=12 \\\\  & x+ky=4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 12 \\\\ 1 & k & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 12 \\\\ 1 & k & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & k & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & k & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4-3k & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+ky=4 \\\\  & (4-3k)y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is consistent dependent if it has infinitely many solutions. For the system to have infinitely many solutions, it must have at least one free variable.\n\nIf $k=\\frac{4}{3},$ then the second equation is $0=0,$ which is true for any value of $y$, and we can remove this equation from the system. As a result, the system will contain only one equation, $x+ky=4.$ \n\nThen, the basic variable will be $x,$ and we will have a free variable $y.$ That means the system will have infinitely many solutions.\n\nTherefore, our system is consistent dependent when $k=\\frac{4}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-131727/selection/e3dbb6296906b72dd0511b45b9171b9cca162c2f0d1c5924ef315cf1c16044f5" :answer/id #uuid "bffb2cb5-dc8d-595a-b9ae-53d24eab107c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131727/selection/fec406b037c336df04ddc47abb8cf02e3ae194404415f3659041d4a99c636727" :answer/id #uuid "12503895-3863-5b7a-90f9-b6b70439dc0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131727/selection/c2e9cbc73ddec801b64583fc77a4e7b9468b8a554c6e72ecc582c1c34171bc66" :answer/id #uuid "7ca1c78d-d02c-5563-8c6b-d09d96b89816" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131727/selection/d8632041aa9cb2a71b6ada1b8f9b15e5f58f906bc98b3276e25ff9a0f4ed73ae" :answer/id #uuid "a56385c6-9689-5117-925e-6bdf347c8be6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131727/selection/99cf9aaf76e0fbfe0a44a681275eb0801b5ea619cac36b3ef641b833f1cadf5f" :answer/id #uuid "f2192a06-07ec-530e-b67e-3bfb1e2b67a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131727/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "47e2311e-69cb-5a3f-99ce-e1179d238593" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131727/selection/fec406b037c336df04ddc47abb8cf02e3ae194404415f3659041d4a99c636727" :answer-field/choices ["q-131727/selection/e3dbb6296906b72dd0511b45b9171b9cca162c2f0d1c5924ef315cf1c16044f5" "q-131727/selection/fec406b037c336df04ddc47abb8cf02e3ae194404415f3659041d4a99c636727" "q-131727/selection/c2e9cbc73ddec801b64583fc77a4e7b9468b8a554c6e72ecc582c1c34171bc66" "q-131727/selection/d8632041aa9cb2a71b6ada1b8f9b15e5f58f906bc98b3276e25ff9a0f4ed73ae" "q-131727/selection/99cf9aaf76e0fbfe0a44a681275eb0801b5ea619cac36b3ef641b833f1cadf5f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131727" :question/id #uuid "d47e9f79-9224-5415-86c6-0753b047d174" :question/math-academy-id "q-131727" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-3y=-1 \\\\  & 4x+3ky=3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 3k & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 3k & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3k+12 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-3y=-1 \\\\ (3k+12)y=7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-4,$ then the second equation is $0=7,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-131727/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "22733f71-de4a-5058-a41c-039e66e333c5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131727"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-74646/selection/4e2429b00a3baaac76f6e33158fbcdff5dcf0af49a1b90a9dac6995df4919225" :answer/id #uuid "a1e1171a-84cd-57a8-a072-8fa3c77d6a38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74646/selection/d8632041aa9cb2a71b6ada1b8f9b15e5f58f906bc98b3276e25ff9a0f4ed73ae" :answer/id #uuid "fb329066-6cb8-5ae7-98d4-7abece7913f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74646/selection/a80a330cf07901aff7b5aa904c4a3541c2351751eef1834664dea83e123d76ff" :answer/id #uuid "253e28e1-1ed1-5ae3-9a70-7506ff88073a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74646/selection/d8a1a66d52573b40c97531ec83902e7d5c053a629619f48b95bf9742d3eabd83" :answer/id #uuid "49af443b-86d7-549e-a16b-7b7eb9af27e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74646/selection/3c752b55a9d477bd0ba6387c5f2201a280295f1502439e3749cf69f3da3e0cae" :answer/id #uuid "54cdb6ed-f055-5f90-8991-c404304e62d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74646/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "aaa208d6-4930-5edd-8817-25def91020ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74646/selection/d8632041aa9cb2a71b6ada1b8f9b15e5f58f906bc98b3276e25ff9a0f4ed73ae" :answer-field/choices ["q-74646/selection/4e2429b00a3baaac76f6e33158fbcdff5dcf0af49a1b90a9dac6995df4919225" "q-74646/selection/d8632041aa9cb2a71b6ada1b8f9b15e5f58f906bc98b3276e25ff9a0f4ed73ae" "q-74646/selection/a80a330cf07901aff7b5aa904c4a3541c2351751eef1834664dea83e123d76ff" "q-74646/selection/d8a1a66d52573b40c97531ec83902e7d5c053a629619f48b95bf9742d3eabd83" "q-74646/selection/3c752b55a9d477bd0ba6387c5f2201a280295f1502439e3749cf69f3da3e0cae"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74646" :question/id #uuid "d0469220-01c3-5e98-b2ee-ca1c1a254981" :question/math-academy-id "q-74646" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+4y=2 \\\\  & 2x+(k+1)y=3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k+1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k+1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & k-7 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+4y=2 \\\\ (k-7)y=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=7,$ then the second equation is $0=-1,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-74646/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "22733f71-de4a-5058-a41c-039e66e333c5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74646"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131731/selection/ac9ae2052cc2e067abcad4ecf5a3f3d17a02fa2d9a881931a644b74ccc7546a6" :answer/id #uuid "7ddc445b-eaf4-5239-b325-e67a7076a111" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131731/selection/d8a1a66d52573b40c97531ec83902e7d5c053a629619f48b95bf9742d3eabd83" :answer/id #uuid "0c29526d-5f05-5fb0-8fd1-80e4970a0ad4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131731/selection/99cf9aaf76e0fbfe0a44a681275eb0801b5ea619cac36b3ef641b833f1cadf5f" :answer/id #uuid "d8ad8605-9941-5e6e-84db-dda2a0900836" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131731/selection/1fdd3d451cdb09e59e0d727552164ce8d6a104bd6e913fd775d21a33e7122eaf" :answer/id #uuid "af1a1043-2e39-53c4-a742-417c2d88b81b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131731/selection/f9a36dc20554097250ff0324e179977bb892219ae9b27b5c2ca8864aac6c0450" :answer/id #uuid "4fef6c43-56bf-5cae-8242-936f5a1353d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131731/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3cbe41d7-612c-5263-adf8-d7662a099b57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131731/selection/1fdd3d451cdb09e59e0d727552164ce8d6a104bd6e913fd775d21a33e7122eaf" :answer-field/choices ["q-131731/selection/ac9ae2052cc2e067abcad4ecf5a3f3d17a02fa2d9a881931a644b74ccc7546a6" "q-131731/selection/d8a1a66d52573b40c97531ec83902e7d5c053a629619f48b95bf9742d3eabd83" "q-131731/selection/99cf9aaf76e0fbfe0a44a681275eb0801b5ea619cac36b3ef641b833f1cadf5f" "q-131731/selection/1fdd3d451cdb09e59e0d727552164ce8d6a104bd6e913fd775d21a33e7122eaf" "q-131731/selection/f9a36dc20554097250ff0324e179977bb892219ae9b27b5c2ca8864aac6c0450"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131731" :question/id #uuid "1faa14aa-cb9d-5c62-96d4-f53593684603" :question/math-academy-id "q-131731" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is consistent dependent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & -2x+6y=-4 \\\\  & 5x+(k-6)y=10\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 5 & k-6 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 5 & k-6 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{5}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 0 & k+9 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & -2x+6y=-4 \\\\  & (k+9)y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is consistent dependent if it has infinitely many solutions. For the system to have infinitely many solutions, it must have at least one free variable.\n\nIf $k=-9,$ then the second equation is $0=0,$ which is true for any value of $y.$ So, we can remove this equation from the system. As a result, the system will contain only one equation, $-2x+6y=-4.$  \n\nThen, the basic variable will be $x,$ and we will have a free variable $y.$ That means the system will have infinitely many solutions.\n\nTherefore, our system is consistent dependent when $k=-9.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-131731/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "22733f71-de4a-5058-a41c-039e66e333c5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131731"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4711"] :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/assets/a50d551e5d8abe8d9ae48778b195c382bbbf96f6fc5083c41b67642e99deffda.png)\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/assets/48c423256fbdc0d7e4f6ff716fb449efe6f98bdf57ba90353bcced930ea4ed17.png)\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/assets/81b7626ac30b06c5eeb10be274dd93476a86dce5fe3053722d96e16b78d7f165.png)\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $z,$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $z$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1-5y \\\\ y=y \\\\ z=3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1-5y \\\\ y \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6173"] :question/problem "Given the system\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/assets/5f1aaf29a3dd8b7ea2c4f7104d532f7b56f32a23ccebbcfa0d1bfe86c772cc5f.png)\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is consistent dependent\n\n- The system has no solution\n\n- The system is consistent independent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/assets/6171d242b0a3887802f629de79cb952d47711a581e88db2d9304a5db356dfb62.png)\n\nUsing Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 6 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/assets/80aff0fd62e3e1aeed17017c864d8d0b875b556ce1a29a89e6c61e632bf9c733.png)\n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\n2x -3y= 4\n$$\n\nThe basic variable is $x,$ and we have a free variable $y.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4712"] :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-2y=1, \\\\ 4x+ky=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/assets/a115d3da691619918bf92d914acdfdd95088e9a141a82ca3fe3230fa7fbb8172.png)\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & k & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & k+4 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/assets/cfea36ae2b5cb5d8715480c1e0ee0b5ba06cf39d0c2032eb6e9b9078bf8c5bde.png)\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-4,$ then the second equation is $0=-5,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-4.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
